    "fileId": 18471,
    "type": "Figure",
    "diagnosis": "Odontogenic myxoma",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "Axial CT showing an expanding mass affecting the maxillary alveolus anteriorly and laterally. The lesion is radiolucent but has irregular thin bony septa at right angles to the cortex, with focal cortical destruction.",
    "source": "Edward W. Odell",
    "copyright": "",
